out:
{salutation},

We are at {place}, {date}. {news}

The road is longer than anyone told us, and dearer. Everything that can be sold to a traveller is sold at twice the price.

Give our love to all at home. I will write again from the land office.

Your affectionate
{sign}

{salutation},

I take up my pen at {place}, {date}, to let you know how we do. {news}

The whole country seems to be going west with us. There is not a tavern without its floor full of movers.

Do not forget us.

Your loving
{sign}

{salutation},

A line from {place}, {date}, in haste. {news}

We think of you all at home more than I can say. Write to us at Bronson, in the Territory of Michigan, where the land office is.

Your affectionate
{sign}

money.halves:
{salutation},

I enclose the first halves of notes to the sum of {amount}, for {what}. The other halves follow by the next mail, so that neither letter alone is worth a thief's trouble.

{news}

Your affectionate
{sign}

money.whole:
{salutation},

I enclose notes to the sum of {amount}, for {what}. I send them whole, and trust to Providence and the mails.

{news}

Your affectionate
{sign}

outcome.pressed:
{to},

The tanner would not wait, and I have had to sell the heifer to meet him. I say no more about the note. Pay it when you can.

{sender}

outcome.sued:
{to},

The bank has brought suit against me as your surety. The sheriff came with the papers on a Saturday, with half the village watching. I will answer it as best I can.

{sender}

outcome.extended:
{to},

The bank has agreed to wait until spring, at interest, and only because the harvest was good. Do not count on such patience twice.

{sender}

outcome.married:
{to},

I do not know how to tell {child} this. With no word from the West since September, the young person has given up waiting, and is to marry the miller's son at Christmas.

{sender}

outcome.posted:
{to},

Mr. Hammond has put your account in the hands of a lawyer in the county town. Your name was read out with the other debtors who have gone west.

{sender}

outcome.patient:
{to},

Mr. Hammond says he will wait for his money. He says it in a way that makes me wish he would not.

{sender}

outcome.named:
{to},

The subscription list was read out at meeting, with the names of those in arrears. Yours was among them.

{sender}
